with a local guard in the same file:

+function isQuizQuestion(value: unknown): value is QuizQuestion {
+  const q = value as Partial<QuizQuestion>;
+  return (
+    typeof q?.question === 'string' &&
+    typeof q?.explanation === 'string' &&
+    Array.isArray(q.options) &&
+    q.options.length > 1 &&
+    q.options.every((o) => typeof o === 'string') &&
+    Number.isInteger(q.correctAnswerIndex) &&
+    (q.correctAnswerIndex as number) >= 0 &&
+    (q.correctAnswerIndex as number) < q.options.length
+  );
+}

This matches the repo's existing 'model output is optional, coerce at the boundary' idiom (src/lib/ai/schemas.ts:85-97 RawBookResponse, applied at src/lib/ai/summarize.ts:22-42). Also tighten the schema at src/lib/ai/schemas.ts:64-72: `minItems: '4', maxItems: '4'` on `options` and `Type.INTEGER` with `minimum: 0, maximum: 3` on `correctAnswerIndex`, so the constraints stop being prose. Risk: a model that violates the invariant now yields fewer questions (or the existing 'Could not generate quiz.' empty state at QuizModal.tsx:125-137) instead of a silently broken card — that is the intended trade. Already-poisoned rows are not repaired by this patch; deleting the book clears them (repo.ts:72).

